<title>CANADA: Canada Jan gas output up 2.8 pct, record exports.</title>
<headline>Canada Jan gas output up 2.8 pct, record exports.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Thursday issued the following data for crude oil and natural gas production and exports:</p>
<p>CRUDE OIL AND EQUIVALENT HYDROCARBONS (thousand cubic meters)</p>
<p>		    Jan 1997     Jan 1996	 pct</p>
<p>   Production   9,880.5	9,721.1	 +1.6</p>
<p>   Exports	5,912.2	5,875.2	 +0.6</p>
<p>   Imports	3,860.1	3,238.9	+19.2</p>
<p>   Ref receipts 8,478.0	7,676.1	+10.4</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS (millions of cubic meters)</p>
<p>		   Jan 1997     Jan 1996	  pct</p>
<p>   Production  14,227.8     13,839.3	  2.8</p>
<p>   Exports	7,730.0	7,146.3	  8.2</p>
<p>   Canada sales 8,517.5	8,742.2	 -2.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Canada sales include direct sales.</p>
<p>Statistics Canada said it was the ninth consecutive monthly year-on-year increase in natural gas output. As for exports, it said it was a continued record, with natural gas from Canada now accounting for almost 13 pct of U.S. consumption.</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Gerard O'Connor, Energy Section, (613) 951-3562.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
